sparky-stereo-skills (0.2.14~dev20261029) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Refresh the public snapshot through ed4e18f (Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os),
    44 skills, 13 more than the published 0.2.10~dev20261022 (4639357):
    - forks-and-online: push the edition's work only to its forks, never
      upstream, keep every branch online the same day, and audit clones for
      work that exists only on one disk;
    - stereo-integrations: the packs that appear with their programs;
    - eleven per-project contribution skills, written from each project's
      public guides and merge records: contrib-ffmpeg, contrib-handbrake,
      contrib-kde, contrib-mkvtoolnix, contrib-mplayer, contrib-mpv,
      contrib-peertube, contrib-qt, contrib-ums, contrib-vlc and
      contrib-x265;
    - new documents: Spatial Roaming Network (a proposal, with its credited
      precedents), Depth inside every window, Dynamic Procedural Foveated
      Rendering, and what stereo costs KWin, measured on the 2016 A10
      laptop;
    - sparky-stereo separates the internal rendering resolution from the
      output resolution and cuts every packing into its native strips;
      depth inside windows is built, with its values, contract and proof;
      the ISO reference of edition-packaging follows the packer; WebXR's
      inline-stereo session mode is recorded.
  * Include what the entries 0.2.11~dev20261023 (1fc1ba5),
    0.2.12~dev20261024 (cc7c2b1) and 0.2.13~dev20261024 (ae030b6) below
    recorded and never published:
    - every domain skill names the Debian packages it needs in
      metadata.requires-packages; sparky-stereo-skills links a domain skill
      only while one of them is installed, unlinks it when none is, and
      keeps the core skills always linked;
    - the helper's package-list checks work with GNU AWK, mawk and BusyBox
      AWK, and the message for a skipped skill is in the nine languages;
    - the package gates were corrected in review, and writing-front-pages is
      a core skill.

