sparky-stereo-skills (0.2.10~dev20261022) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Refresh the public snapshot through 4639357 (Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os),
    31 skills:
    - three new skills: stereo-serving (a server or caster sends each
      device its own frame format at the raster it declares, never the
      desktop's full side by side), kde-desktop-defaults (Plasma search
      defaults, the task manager, frozen-window recovery and
      removable-drive formatting) and user-groups (the groups every
      desktop user gets);
    - the packaging rules are public in edition-packaging: provenance,
      Paweł's formula, rebuilt upstream packages, the signed repository
      and how a change is published, and packing the ISO;
    - MPEG-2 has its own 3D mark, the JP3D user data;
    - a program never touches the user's file on its own, and the
      definitive eye swap is the output's;
    - X11 views at another size than their resolution;
    - consult a local reference index before the web or memory;
    - long sections of stereo-video, lean-code and edition-packaging move
      to references, so each skill's selected context fits the default
      size again; the Lean Code status is brought up to date.
  * The source package rebuilds without the public checkout: the checkout
    is needed only when no snapshot is bundled.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:18:11 -0300

sparky-stereo-skills (0.2.9~dev20261022) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Refresh the public snapshot through 0e0b3a2 (Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os):
    full side by side is the layout and any resolution per eye is the pact,
    each eye at the resolution it has (a half top-and-bottom 1920x1080 frame
    is one 3840x540 picture), and Stereo KWin resizes once at the output;
    unpacking costs nothing, a second resize costs twice; the
